Group 3 -  Diagnostic Evidence Team (DET)**  
 Member 1 (**Radiologist (Lead)**): Evaluates any imaging studies that may be relevant to diagnosing conditions that could mimic shingles or identify other causes of pain and rash.
 Member 2 (**Neurologist**): Assesses any potential neurological implications from the shingles infection, including nerve pain and sensitization, leading to further diagnostics or therapeutic interventions as necessary.
 Member 3 (**Laboratory Medicine Specialist**): Oversees the interpretation of any necessary lab tests, including serology for varicella

Group 4 -  Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)**  
 Member 1 (**Senior Consultant in Infectious Diseases (Lead)**): Provides overarching guidance based on the collective findings of the Initial Assessment Team and Diagnostic Evidence Team, synthesizing clinical insights into a cohesive treatment plan.
 Member 2 (**Clinical Decision Specialist**): Coordinates recommendations from the various teams, ensuring multidisciplinary opinions are integrated into the final treatment strategy.
 Member 3 (**Clinical Pharmacist**): Evaluates proposed medication regimens post


